OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0       ju
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,5,GMAJOR UNVEILS HIS "BUDGET FOR SAVERS"
OL,7, 404FRadical change to taxes on savings
OL,9, 414 INCOME TAXFAllowances scaled up
OL,10, 410 STAMP DUTYFended but only on shares
OL,12, 411 PETROLFand DERV duty increased
OL,13, 412 ALCOHOLFand cigarettes to go up
OL,15, 413 FOOTBALLFclubs' improvement aid
OL,16, 416 NURSERIESFWorkplace tax exemption
OL,17,Qppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,19, 440 ANALYSISFThe microscope on Major
OL,21, 420 REACTIONFCity and political comment
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49604
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                  G4/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GA BUDGET FOR
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GSAVERS
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, Chancellor John Major said that his
OL,7, first Budget would be, above all,
OL,8, a Budget for savers.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FHe went on to announce the abolition of
OL,11,Fcomposite rate tax on bank and building
OL,12,Fsociety deposits from 6 April 1991.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FMr Major also announced a wholly new
OL,15,Ftax incentive - the Tax Exempt Special
OL,16,FSavings Account.
OL,18,FEvery adult would be entitled to one
OL,19,FTESSA, with tax-free interest on a sum
OL,20,Fbetween #150 and #1,800 invested
OL,21,Fmonthly over five years
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49605
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                  G5/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GNON-TAXPAYER SAVERS
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GTO BENEFIT
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,5,F
OL,6, After the abolition of composite rate
OL,7, tax, tax will be still be deducted from
OL,8, bank and building society interest, but
OL,9, at the higher basic rate.
OL,11,FFrom 6 April 1991 tax will fall on only
OL,12,Fthose who should pay it - and not
OL,13,Fon those who should not, Mr Major said.
OL,15,FA scheme of self-certification was
OL,16,Fenvisaged, allowing non-taxpayers to
OL,17,Freceive gross interest. Non-taxpayers
OL,18,Fwould also be able to reclaim tax.
OL,20,FThe change will help millions of
OL,21,Fsmall savers, Mr Major said.
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49606
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                  G6/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GTAX ALLOWANCES
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GUPRATED
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, The Chancellor has said he does not
OL,7, intend to change either the basic or
OL,8, higher tax rates at this stage.
OL,10,FBut personal tax allowances will be
OL,11,Fuprated by the statutory indexation
OL,12,Ffactor of 7.7%, rounded up.
OL,14,FThe personal allowance will rise by
OL,15,F#220 to #3,005 while the new married
OL,16,Fcouple's allowance will be #1,720. The
OL,17,F#20,700 higher rate threshold remains.
OL,19,FThe additional personal allowance for
OL,20,Fsingle parents and the widow's
OL,21,Fbereavement allowance is also #1,720.
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49607
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                  G7/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GTAX ALLOWANCES
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GUPRATED
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, Tax allowances for the elderly will be
OL,7, fully uprated in line with inflation,
OL,8, Mr Major said.
OL,10,FFor those aged 65 to 74, the personal
OL,11,Fallowance goes up #270 to #3,670 and
OL,12,Fthe married couple's allowance #160 to
OL,13,F#2,145.
OL,15,FFor those aged 75 and over, the
OL,16,Fpersonal allowance increases by #280
OL,17,Fto #3,820 and the married couple's
OL,18,Fallowance rises to #2,185.
OL,20,FThe income limit for these allowances
OL,21,Fis to be fully indexed to #12,300.
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49608
SC,0008
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                  G8/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GTAX ALLOWANCES
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GUPRATED
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, The Inheritance Tax Threshold will be
OL,7, raised by #10,000 to #128,000 in line
OL,8, with inflation.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe Capital Gains Tax exemption, which
OL,11,Fis currently #5,000, will remain at
OL,12,Fthis level.
OL,14,FBut Mr Major pointed out that married
OL,15,Fcouples were now entitled to two
OL,16,Fexempt amounts, effectively giving a
OL,17,Fmarried couple an exemption of #10,000.
OL,22,Q]G This Ceefax page is fromF20-03-90
OL,23,Q]G Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49609
SC,0009
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                  G9/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GSTAMP DUTY ON SHARE
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GDEALINGS TO GO
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, Stamp duty on share dealings and Stamp
OL,7, Duty Reserve Tax are to be abolished
OL,8, late in 1991/92.
OL,10,FThe abolitions will be timed as nearly
OL,11,Fas possible to coincide with the
OL,12,Fintroduction of paperless dealing, the
OL,13,FChancellor said.
OL,15,FThis will help secure the UK's position
OL,16,Fas a leading financial centre, he added
OL,17,F
OL,18,FBut he emphasised that stamp duty on
OL,19,Fland and property would be unaffected
OL,20,Fby this measure.
OL,22,Q]G This Ceefax page is fromF20-03-90
OL,23,Q]G Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49610
SC,0010
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                 G10/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GDUTY INCREASED
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GON PETROL
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, The Chancellor has increased the excise
OL,7, duty on petrol and DERV by 10%.
OL,9,FThis means an extra 9p per gallon on
OL,10,FDERV, 11p on leaded petrol, and 9p on
OL,11,Funleaded petrol; Mr Major said unleaded
OL,12,Fpetrol now took 30% of the market.
OL,14,FVehicle Excise Duty on cars, buses,
OL,15,Fcoaches, taxis and many lorries will
OL,16,Fbe unchanged.
OL,18,FMr Major said he would also eliminate
OL,19,Fa further 188 VED rates for lorries in
OL,20,Fan attempt to simplify the system.
OL,22,Q]G This Ceefax page is fromF20-03-90
OL,23,Q]G Much more at: teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49611
SC,0011
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                 G11/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GCIGARETTES AND
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GALCOHOL GO UP
OL,4,F        Q(.%
OL,6, Alcohol duties go up at 1800 today;
OL,7, with one exception, these will go up in
OL,8, line with inflation.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThis will put 7p on a bottle of table
OL,11,Fwine, and 2p on a pint of beer.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FBut spirits, which have enjoyed a duty
OL,14,Fstandstill since 1985, will see a 10%
OL,15,Frise, increasing the price of a bottle
OL,16,Fof spirits by 54p.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FDuty on cigarettes and cigars will go
OL,19,Fup by 10% from midnight on Thursday.
OL,20,FThis means 20 cigarettes will go up by
OL,21,F10p. There is no rise for pipe tobacco.
OL,22,F
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49612
SC,0012
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                 G12/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GMAJOR ANNOUNCES HELP
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GFOR FOOTBALL
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, Football pool betting duty is to come
OL,7, down from 42.5% to 40% with the proviso
OL,8, that savings go towards improved safety
OL,10,FThe full amount of the savings offered
OL,11,Fmust be passed by the pools promoters
OL,12,Fto the Football Trust and used to
OL,13,Fimprove safety at football grounds.
OL,15,FThe measure was designed to help clubs
OL,16,Fcarry out the safety improvements
OL,17,Fsuggested in the Taylor report after
OL,18,Fthe Bradford and Hillsborough tragedies
OL,20,FTax allowances would only help the few
OL,21,Fprofitable clubs, the Chancellor said.
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49613
SC,0013
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Qk5    j5      |                 G13/30
OL,2,Qk4j5~k5~k5{5%GWORKPLACE NURSERIES
OL,3,Qz5oz5z5z5op0 GEXEMPTED
OL,4,         Q(.%
OL,6, The Chancellor said an increasing
OL,7, number of mothers wanted to return to
OL,8, work and employers wanted to help this.
OL,10,FEmployers complained that the taxation
OL,11,Fof workplace nurseries as benefits in
OL,12,Fkind obstructed the growth of nursery
OL,13,Fprovision and recruitment, while women
OL,14,Fsaw it as a disincentive to work.
OL,16,FHe had therefore decided to exempt the
OL,17,Fvalue of workplace nurseries and
OL,18,Fplaygroups from taxation as a benefit.
OL,20,FThis action would come into force from
OL,21,FApril 6 this year.
OL,23,Q]GFromF20-03-90G/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
