OL,3,Vj5op0z5z5j5j5op0p`ppppppppppppppp
OL,5,GCHANCELLOR DELIVERS "BUDGET FOR SAVERS"
OL,7, 103FNew tax-free accounts announced
OL,8, 104FMajor stands firm on interest rates
OL,9, 105FKinnock welcomes tax concessions
OL,11, 401FBudget Headlines    G420FReaction
OL,12, 440FBudget Analysis     G498FMeasures
OL,13,Tppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,15, 114 POLL TAXFMore Conservatives resign
OL,16,F
OL,17, 111 SHORTSFIRA planted bombs at factory
OL,19, 108 ISRAELFPeres to form government
OL,21, 110 FRAUDFFourteen arrested after raids
OL,23,T]FFromG20-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49615
SC,0015
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Vk4                              G15/30
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMAJOR DELIVERS HIS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGBUDGET FOR SAVERS
OL,4,D
OL,5, Chancellor of the Exchequer John Major
OL,6, has given what he called a Budget for
OL,7, Savers in the House of Commons - the
OL,8, first to be seen live on TV.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FIn an 81-minute speech he announced new
OL,11,Fsavings accounts in which interest
OL,12,Fwould be tax-free as long as capital
OL,13,Fwas left for five years.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FStamp duty on share dealing is being
OL,16,Fabolished and workplace nurseries will
OL,17,Fno longer be taxed as a perk.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FExcise duty on wine, spirits and
OL,20,Fcigarettes are up broadly in line with
OL,21,Finflation. Car tax discs stay at #100.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]FFromG20-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49616
SC,0016
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Vk4                              G16/30
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGMAJOR SAYS NO CHANGE IN
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGINTEREST RATE POLICY
OL,4,D
OL,5, Chancellor of the Exchequer John Major
OL,6, said he was aware of the distress high
OL,7, interest rates were causing.
OL,9,FBut he said credit controls would not
OL,10,Fwork in the modern world in anything
OL,11,Fbut the short term. They would replace
OL,12,Fhome borrowing with overseas borrowing.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FHe also announced new help for soccer
OL,15,Fgrounds. The tax on pools is to be
OL,16,Fcut from 42.5% to 40% - the savings
OL,17,Fgoing to improve ground safety.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FThe change is for five years and is
OL,20,Fexpected to yield #100m. It will then
OL,21,Fbe reviewed, Mr Major said.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]FFromG20-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49617
SC,0017
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Vk4                              G17/30
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGKINNOCK WELCOMES BUDGET
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTAX CONCESSIONS
OL,4,D
OL,5, Opposition leader Neil Kinnock welcomed
OL,6, the tax relief on workplace nurseries
OL,7, and the VAT relief on bad debts in John
OL,8, Major's first Budget.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FHe said it showed the first signs that
OL,11,Fthe Government was beginning to listen.
OL,13,FNear the end of his speech Mr Major was
OL,14,Finterrupted by Scottish Labour MPs who
OL,15,Fwanted to know how higher savings
OL,16,Flimits for poll tax benefit would
OL,17,Faffect Scots already paying the tax.
OL,19,FLabour has indicated that it will fight
OL,20,Fthe decision not to backdate the raised
OL,21,Fsavings limit for Scotland.
OL,23,T]FFromG20-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49618
SC,0018
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Vk4                              G18/30
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGTORY MAYOR RESIGNS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGOVER POLL TAX
OL,4,D
OL,5, The Tory major of St Austell, Cornwall,
OL,6, has resigned from the party in protest
OL,7, at the community charge.
OL,9,FEarlier 9 Conservative councillors in
OL,10,FHumberside resigned the party whip.
OL,12,FThe councillors, who represent the
OL,13,Fvillage of Cottingham on Beverly
OL,14,FBorough Council, said the application
OL,15,Fof the #373 tax was unfair.
OL,17,FConservative party chairman Kenneth
OL,18,FBaker said it was particularly sad that
OL,19,Fthe councillors had been pushed into
OL,20,Fthis by the overspending of the Labour-
OL,21,Fcontrolled Humberside County Council.
OL,23,T]FFromG20-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49619
SC,0019
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Vk4                              G19/30
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFIVE INJURED IN SHORTS
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGFACTORY EXPLOSIONS
OL,5, Five people have been hurt in two
OL,6, explosions at a Shorts missile factory
OL,7, in Belfast.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe explosions took place close to a
OL,10,Fbuilding at the back of an annexe to
OL,11,FCastlereagh Further Education College,
OL,12,Fwhich shares the site.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FThe IRA has said that it planted the
OL,15,Ftwo bombs at the factory, which makes
OL,16,Fmissiles for the Ministry of Defence.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FNorthern Ireland minister John Cope
OL,19,Fsaid it was an IRA attack on jobs, on
OL,20,Finvestment, on working people and on
OL,21,Fstudents.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]FFromG20-03-90F/ teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,497,190,120,250,0,100
PN,49620
SC,0020
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F496A1774021955
OL,1,Vk4                              G20/30
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGPERES TO FORM NEXT
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGISRAELI GOVERNMENT
OL,4,D
OL,5, The leader of Israel's Labour party,
OL,6, Shimon Peres, has been asked to form
OL,7, the next Israeli government.
OL,9,FMr Peres will replace Likud leader
OL,10,FYitzhak Shamir whose coalition with
OL,11,Fthe Labour party collapsed last week
OL,12,Fafter a vote of no-confidence.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FUnder Israeli law the President had to
OL,15,Fdecide who would form the next
OL,16,Fgovernment because parliament could not
OL,17,Fdecide between the two main parties.
OL,19,FThe split between them came about
OL,20,Fbecause Likud would not accept Middle
OL,21,FEast peace proposals from the US.
